Description: native YTP/1 stealth transport command-line client
 YUME provides authenticated TLS 1.3 HTTP/2 transport with composite
 Ed25519 and ML-DSA-87 identities, hybrid session establishment and
 directional key epochs. The native client supports SOCKS5 TCP and UDP.
 .
 This experimental package includes schema-1 setup and validation tools.
 It does not provide the transport-v2 desktop consumer or a frozen C ABI.

Package: yume-daemon
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libssl3t64 (>= 3.5.0),
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Suggests:
 ssl-cert
Description: authenticated stealth transport server daemon
 YUME serves native YTP/1 sessions and ordinary HTTP cover traffic through
 its TLS front door. Authenticated clients receive explicitly configured
 direct TCP and UDP access.
 .
 This package contains the yumed server daemon, a disabled-by-default
 systemd service, a locked service user, and a schema-1 configuration.
 Operators must provision credentials and a cover site before enabling it.
